# With @repair, every error the tolerant parse repairs past is a
# diagnostic: separate mistakes give one each, and the errors one mistake
# sets off (`f(a b c d)`, three deletions in a row) give one.
initialize
open errors.tally
| let a = 1 +
| let b = 2
| let c = ) 3
| let d = 4
| f(a b c d)
change errors.tally
| let a = 1 +
| let b = 2
